Package: spikedGLHT
Type: Package
Title: General Linear Hypothesis Tests with Spiked Noise Covariance
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(person("Haoran", "Li", email = "hzl0152@auburn.edu",
    role = c("aut", "cre")), person("Alexander", "Aue", role = "ctb"),
    person("Debashis", "Paul", role = "ctb"), person("Jie", "Peng", role = "ctb"))
Description: Regularized likelihood ratio, Lawley-Hotelling, and
    Bartlett-Nanda-Pillai tests for general linear hypotheses in
    high-dimensional multivariate regression with spiked noise covariance.
    Implements bias-adjusted covariance estimation, minimax regularization,
    data-driven spike selection, and normal or parametric bootstrap calibration
    following Li, Aue, Paul, and Peng (2024) <doi:10.1080/01621459.2023.2278825>.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: quadprog, stats
Suggests: RMTstat
URL: https://github.com/HaoranLi/spikedGLHT
BugReports: https://github.com/HaoranLi/spikedGLHT/issues
